{{!-- The neighbouring communities — each a headed row carrying its two facts and the notes kept on
      it. Shared by the steading's Places tab and the steadfast sheet.
      Params: title, places (NeighborPlace snapshots), showNames, showTravel, editableSize.

      The GROUP takes the section heading and its rule; a place's own name sits a level below it. Five
      sibling headings with nothing naming them is what this used to be, and "Marshedge" says what it
      is only to someone who already knows.

      Each of the three flags marks a place where the two sheets genuinely differ, rather than a
      style choice:

      `showNames` is false on the steading, where those pools are rendered in Folk's reference column
      as individually clickable entries; a second, inert copy of the same words would be the wall
      that tab exists to retire. The steadfast is a definition with no roster to click into, so it
      keeps the plain list.

      `editableSize` is true only on the steadfast. Size is DEFINITIONAL — the book's tier word for
      the place — so it is authored where the definition lives and kept in step there by
      migrateNeighborPlaces, which would silently revert an edit made anywhere else. The steading
      reads the word and nothing more.

      `showTravel` is the exact opposite, and true only on the steading: travel is measured FROM
      HERE, so it is not a fact about the neighbour and a steadfast a dozen places sit at cannot
      state it. It is free text because the book states it in prose and inconsistently ("About 15
      miles", "a long day's march") — really a Chart a Course answer that moves with route and
      season. --}}
<section class="steading-neighbor-places">
	{{#if title}}{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=title}}{{/if}}
	{{#each places}}
		<section class="steading-neighbor-place steading-block">
			<div class="steading-neighbor-head">
				<h4 class="steading-neighbor-name">{{name}}{{#if (hasText subtitle)}} <span class="steading-neighbor-subtitle">{{subtitle}}</span>{{/if}}</h4>
				{{!-- The facts sit on a rule at the right of the heading — the sheet's one idiom for a
				      value — and a fact with nothing in it is left out rather than drawn empty. The
				      steadfast sheet is the exception and always draws both, because it is where they are
				      authored: a field you cannot see is a field you cannot fill in. --}}
				<div class="steading-neighbor-facts">
					{{#if ../editableSize}}
						{{!-- Always drawn here: this is where a Size is CHOSEN. A select with nothing
						      matching would silently show its first option, so a place whose Size nobody has
						      chosen would read as "hamlet" — the snapshot supplies a blank leading option
						      instead. Bound by class on the steadfast item sheet rather than stamped with a
						      data-change-action: that vocabulary belongs to the ACTOR sheets' router, and no
						      steading routes this one — a steading never writes a neighbour's Size. --}}
						<span class="steading-neighbor-fact">
							<span class="steading-neighbor-fact-label">{{localize "stonetop.steading.neighbors.size"}}</span>
							<select class="steading-neighbor-size-select" data-id="{{slug}}"
							        aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.a11y.neighborSize' place=name}}"
							        {{#unless @root.editable}}disabled{{/unless}}>
								{{#each sizeOptions}}
									<option value="{{value}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{label}}</option>
								{{/each}}
							</select>
						</span>
					{{else if (hasText sizeLabel)}}
						{{!-- A fact with nothing in it is not a fact. The groupings among these rows are
						      regions rather than steadings and the book gives them no size at all, so the
						      label and an em dash would be two pieces of furniture saying nothing. --}}
						<span class="steading-neighbor-fact">
							<span class="steading-neighbor-fact-label">{{localize "stonetop.steading.neighbors.size"}}</span>
							<span class="steading-neighbor-fact-value">{{sizeLabel}}</span>
						</span>
					{{/if}}
					{{#if (or ../editableTravel (and ../showTravel (hasText travel)))}}
						<span class="steading-neighbor-fact">
							<span class="steading-neighbor-fact-label">{{localize "stonetop.steading.neighbors.travel"}}</span>
							<input type="text" class="steading-neighbor-travel" data-change-action="neighborPlaceTravel" data-id="{{slug}}"
							       value="{{travel}}" aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.a11y.neighborTravel' place=name}}">
						</span>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
			</div>
			{{!-- The shared grow-field: it wraps, breaks a long unbroken word rather than running off
			      the side, and gets taller as the note does. A note about a neighbour is written over a
			      campaign, so a fixed box would scroll its own beginning out of sight. --}}
			<label class="steading-neighbor-text-field">
				<span>{{localize "stonetop.steading.neighbors.notes"}}</span>
				<textarea rows="2" class="stonetop-neighbor-place-note stonetop-grow-field"
				          data-change-action="neighborPlaceNote" data-id="{{slug}}"
				          placeholder="{{localize 'stonetop.steading.neighbors.notes'}}">{{note}}</textarea>
			</label>
			{{#if (and ../showNames names)}}
				<div class="steading-neighbor-text-field">
					<span>{{localize "stonetop.steading.neighbors.names"}}</span>
					<p class="steading-names-text">{{names}}</p>
				</div>
			{{/if}}
		</section>
	{{/each}}
</section>
